<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8'?>
<graphml xmlns="http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns/1.0/graphml.xsd">
  <key id="d6" for="edge" attr.name="source_id" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d5" for="edge" attr.name="keywords" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d4" for="edge" attr.name="description" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d3" for="edge" attr.name="weight" attr.type="double" />
  <key id="d2" for="node" attr.name="source_id" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d1" for="node" attr.name="description" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d0" for="node" attr.name="entity_type" attr.type="string" />
  <graph edgedefault="undirected">
    <node id="&quot;HMS BUTTERCUP&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"HMS Buttercup is a Flower-class corvette built during World War II, known for its role in convoy escort duties and its significance in the war effort."&lt;SEP&gt;"HMS Buttercup is a ship that has witnessed the horrors of war and emerged stronger, symbolizing resilience and sacrifice."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0113</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HARLAND AND WOLFF SHIPYARD&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Harland and Wolff shipyard is the site where HMS Buttercup's keel was laid in 1941, located in Belfast, Northern Ireland."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0113</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BRITISH ROYAL NAVY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The British Royal Navy is the organization responsible for the construction and operation of HMS Buttercup, playing a crucial role in the war effort."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0113</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FLOWER-CLASS CORVETTES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Flower-class corvettes are a class of warships built during World War II, including HMS Buttercup, designed to protect convoys and disrupt enemy supply lines."&lt;SEP&gt;"Flower-class corvettes are a type of warship built during World War II, designed to combat the German U-boat threat in the Atlantic."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0113</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GERMAN U-BOAT THREAT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The German U-boat threat is the primary naval challenge faced by the Flower-class corvettes, including HMS Buttercup, during World War II."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0113</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BRITISH NATIONAL ARCHIVES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The British National Archives holds records related to the construction of HMS Buttercup and other Flower-class corvettes."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0113</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DR. ERIC GROVE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Dr. Eric Grove is a naval historian and author who has written about the Royal Navy since 1815, providing insights into the historical context of HMS Buttercup."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0113</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CAPTAIN JOHN RODGAARD&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Captain John Rodgaard is a retired Royal Navy officer and expert on World War II naval history, offering commentary on the significance of HMS Buttercup's construction."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0113</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TOM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Tom is a person who feels a sense of pride and purpose after a significant moment, connected to the HMS Buttercup."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tom is a young sailor on board the HMS Buttercup, joining the crew in 1941 and experiencing the realities of wartime service."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0113</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LIEUTENANT THOMPSON&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lieutenant Thompson is a member of the HMS Buttercup's crew who dies during a watch, prompting a respectful cremation ceremony."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0113</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COMMANDER JAMESON&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Commander Jameson is the captain of the HMS Buttercup, overseeing the cremation ceremony for Lieutenant Thompson."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0113</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BELFAST, NORTHERN IRELAND&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Belfast, Northern Ireland is the city where the HMS Buttercup was constructed at the Harland and Wolff shipyard."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0113</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NORTH ATLANTIC&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The North Atlantic is the ocean where the HMS Buttercup operates, conducting convoy escort duties during World War II."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0113</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FEBRUARY 17, 1941&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"February 17, 1941 is the date when the keel laying ceremony for HMS Buttercup took place at the Harland and Wolff shipyard in Belfast, Northern Ireland."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0113</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WORLD WAR II&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"World War II is the broader historical context in which HMS Buttercup was constructed and operated, involving significant naval warfare."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0113</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CONVOY ESCORT DUTIES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ROLE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Convoy escort duties are the primary missions assigned to HMS Buttercup and other Flower-class corvettes, ensuring the safety of merchant ships."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0113</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SONAR TECHNOLOGY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sonar technology is an advanced feature of the Flower-class corvettes, including HMS Buttercup, used to detect and track enemy submarines."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0113</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ALLIED WAR EFFORT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Allied war effort includes the construction and operation of HMS Buttercup and other warships to counter the German naval threat."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0113</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MERCHANT SHIPS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Merchant ships are the cargo vessels escorted by HMS Buttercup and other corvettes to ensure safe passage through dangerous waters."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0113</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GERMAN NAVAL THREAT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The German naval threat, particularly the U-boat threat, is the primary adversary faced by HMS Buttercup and other Allied warships during World War II."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0113</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BELFAST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Belfast is the city where the HMS Buttercup was constructed at the Harland and Wolff shipyard."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0113</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NORTHERN IRELAND&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Northern Ireland is the region where the HMS Buttercup was constructed at the Harland and Wolff shipyard."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0113</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHOPPY WATERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Choppy waters are the conditions in which the HMS Buttercup operates, particularly in the North Atlantic during wartime."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0113</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SAILORS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sailors are the crew members of the HMS Buttercup, including experienced veterans and young recruits, tasked with various duties during wartime operations."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0113</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;YOUNG RECRUITS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Young recruits are new members of the HMS Buttercup's crew, such as Tom, who are learning the ropes of life at sea."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0113</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SUNSET&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sunset is mentioned as a time when the crew of the HMS Buttercup stands watch, symbolizing the end of another day of service."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0113</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CREMATION CEREMONY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A cremation ceremony is held for Lieutenant Thompson, a member of the HMS Buttercup's crew, to honor his sacrifice."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0113</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HONOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Honor is a theme that runs through the narrative, representing the respect and reverence shown to fallen comrades."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0113</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SACRIFICE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sacrifice is a significant theme, highlighting the personal and collective sacrifices made by those serving on the HMS Buttercup."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0113</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PRIDE AND PURPOSE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pride and purpose are feelings experienced by the crew of the HMS Buttercup, reflecting their sense of duty and accomplishment."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0113</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WAR EFFORT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"War effort is the overarching goal of the HMS Buttercup and other Allied warships, contributing to the broader struggle against the Axis powers."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0113</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FRONT LINES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Front Lines refer to the battlefield where sacrifices were made, symbolizing the place of intense combat and service."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0113</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ASHES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Ashes represent the end of a battle or a significant event, symbolizing the conclusion of a period of conflict."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0113</data>
    </node>
